# Light Assistant Project Overview

## Project Description
Light Assistant is a full-stack application for controlling and monitoring lighting systems, with a focus on DJ and entertainment environments. It combines hardware control with a modern web interface.

## Repository Structure

### Frontend ([src/](mdc:src))
- [src/app/](mdc:src/app) - Next.js application pages and routes
- [src/components/](mdc:src/components) - Reusable React components
- [src/contexts/](mdc:src/contexts) - React context providers
- [src/hooks/](mdc:src/hooks) - Custom React hooks
- [src/websocket-server/](mdc:src/websocket-server) - WebSocket server for real-time communication

### Hardware ([hardware/](mdc:hardware))
- [hardware/dj-spl-meter/](mdc:hardware/dj-spl-meter) - SPL meter implementation
- [hardware/firmware/](mdc:hardware/firmware) - Device firmware
- [hardware/enclosure/](mdc:hardware/enclosure) - Hardware enclosure designs
- [hardware/kicad/](mdc:hardware/kicad) - PCB and schematic files

### Documentation
- [docs/](mdc:docs) - Project documentation
- [README.md](mdc:README.md) - Getting started guide

## Key Technologies
- Next.js for the web application
- TypeScript for type safety
- Tailwind CSS for styling
- WebSocket for real-time communication
- ESPHome for hardware control

